# Files in this repo that are NOT part of the published site.
#
# The assets directory is the repository root (same as the Netlify publish
# directory), so everything not listed here would be served. `modules.json`
# stays public deliberately: it is the fallback catalogue data, and the
# Netlify deploy published it too.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.freebuff/
.wrangler/
node_modules/

netlify/
tools/

README.md
LICENSE
package.json
server.js
wrangler.toml
.assetsignore
# The function Pages compiles at deploy time. The upload is a staged copy of the
# repository, so without this rule the router and the catch-all would also be
# published as files under /functions/.
functions/
# Deploy files: the script that stages the upload and the staging output it
# writes (`.pages-dist/`) are development files. The assets directory is the
# repository root, so anything not listed here would be uploaded and served.
.pages-dist/
